ub-pkg-manager for Debian
==========================

This package provides the UB OS Component management tools.

Building the Package
--------------------

To build the Debian packages:

1. Install build dependencies:
   sudo apt-get install debhelper-compat dh-python python3-all python3-setuptools

2. Build the package:
   dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

3. Check with lintian:
   lintian -i -I --show-overrides ../ub-pkg-manager_*.changes

Package Structure
-----------------

This source package builds four binary packages:

* ub-pkg-manager - Main package with core functionality
* ub-pkg-urma - UnifiedBus Communication function management
* ub-pkg-mem - UnifiedBus Pooled Memory function management
* ub-pkg-virt - UnifiedBus Device Virtualization function management

Build Process
-------------

The build process follows these steps:
1. Extract source tarball (ub-pkg-manager-1.0.0.tar.gz)
2. Apply patches (0001-update-libobmm-to-obmm.patch)
3. Build Python package using setuptools
4. Install files to appropriate locations
5. Create systemd service units
6. Package into .deb files

Services
--------

Each package installs a systemd service that:
- Is enabled and started on installation (if not in a container)
- Is stopped and disabled on removal (if not in a container)
- Detects container environments to avoid service management issues

Configuration
-------------

Configuration files are installed to:
- /etc/ub-pkg-manager/check.yml (main configuration)
- /usr/local/ub-pkg-manager/bin/ (management scripts)

